## Base configuration. augenrules concatenates rules.d/*.rules in lexical
## order into /etc/audit/audit.rules, which auditd loads at boot.

# Start from an empty rule set.
-D
# Kernel buffer for events waiting to be read by auditd.
-b 8192
# If the kernel cannot record an event (backlog full, auditd dead), print a
# message (1). 2 would panic the machine, which some accreditation schemes
# require: an unaudited system must stop. Panic is a denial-of-service lever
# for anyone who can generate events quickly, so it is not used here.
-f 1
# Wait up to 60 s for space in the backlog before dropping an event.
--backlog_wait_time 60000
# Ignore errors from rules referring to paths or syscalls that do not exist
# on this architecture, so one file works on x86_64 and aarch64.
-i
